    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939221
    m_Localized: 01 / First harvest
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939222
    m_Localized: "Start on one grass plot with no inventory. Grass matures naturally.
      Run harvest() until you own five hay, then research Loops. Load First harvest
      from Templates.\n\nNext research Operators, Variables, Sensors and Planting.
      Research does not happen just because you own enough resources: select a node
      and pay, or later use unlock(). Free grass and bushes provide recovery if you
      run out of crop seeds.\n\nThis campaign aims at about three hours of game time
      to full research with a working automated strategy. Your planning and editing
      time is additional. Research speed bonuses are part of normal 1\xD7 play; the
      Settings speed multiplier accelerates the entire world."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939223
    m_Localized: 02 / Programs & states
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939224
    m_Localized: 'Programs are reusable modules. The library shows a card for every
      file, a total count, active-file count and drone-slot usage. Green means the
      file has running workers; an amber border means it is open in the main editor.
      A file may be both running and selected. Paused tasks remain active; idle files
      have no live workers.


      Edit switches the main editor without stopping
      existing work. Main Run replaces the current controller and its workers. Window
      opens a draggable editor; Run separately launches that file if a drone slot
      is free. Stop all terminates every worker. Closing an editor window leaves
      its code and running tasks intact. Running files cannot be deleted; at least
      one file is retained.


      Use Cmd/Ctrl+Z to undo and Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+Z to
      redo. F9 toggles a breakpoint at the caret line. Pause, Step and the variable
      watch help diagnose a program.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939225
    m_Localized: 03 / Language essentials
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939226
    m_Localized: 'The interpreter uses Python-inspired syntax, not a full Python
      installation. Indent blocks with four spaces or one tab; do not mix them. Names
      and enum members are case-sensitive. Research the corresponding language nodes
      before using variables, branches, functions or collections. Unrestricted syntax
      in Settings removes language gates only; it does not grant crops or research.


      Supported
      forms include if/elif/else, while, for, break/continue, parameterized functions,
      default arguments, return, global, imports, lists, immutable tuples, sets,
      dictionaries, indexing, unpacking and closures. Python standard-library modules
      and operating-system access are unavailable. Compare with ==, assign with =;
      negative indices count from the end.


      Use print() during debugging,
      but frequent printing adds execution cost. A while loop without an exit continues
      until Stop; prefer inventory-based goals for finite jobs.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939227
    m_Localized: 04 / Staged research
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939228
    m_Localized: "Research has three independent requirements: prior discoveries,
      cumulative production and a payable resource cost. Production totals count
      successful harvests even after you spend the resources; they are not a second
      payment. The tree shows current / required totals. Completing a crop unlocks
      further field, speed and yield tiers.\n\nField sizes: Planting \u2192 2\xD72;
      Trees \u2192 4\xD74; Pumpkins \u2192 8\xD78; Cacti \u2192 16\xD716; Tail exploration
      \u2192 32\xD732. You still pay for each expansion. Existing purchased research
      is retained when updating; start a new farm to experience the complete staged
      campaign.\n\nget_cost() reports the price, get_unlock_requirements() reports
      gates, and can_unlock() checks both gates and funds. unlock() returns False
      without spending when any requirement is missing. There is no elapsed-time
      certification gate. The tier lists below identify the discovery needed for
      each upgrade."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939229
    m_Localized: 05 / Crop supply chains
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939230
    m_Localized: 'Grass yields hay. Bushes and trees yield wood. Carrots require
      tilled soil, hay and wood; pumpkins and sunflowers use carrots; cacti use pumpkins.
      Research increases seed costs as well as yields. Inspect get_cost(Entities.Carrot)
      before filling a field, and reserve enough inputs for multiple repair cycles.


      Planting
      needs an empty compatible plot; dead pumpkins can be replaced directly. till()
      switches ground type. Clearing or expanding resets the field and loses standing
      plants. Protect your inventory before switching the whole field to another
      crop.


      Trees grow more slowly for every adjacent tree, so alternate
      trees and bushes in a checkerboard. Normal field edges wrap: East from the
      last column returns to column zero. Maze and tail mode do not wrap. Base growth
      times are grass 3s, bush 4s, tree 6s, carrot 7s, pumpkin 11s, sunflower 8.5s
      and cactus 1.5s; water speeds growth.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939231
    m_Localized: 06 / Water & infection
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939232
    m_Localized: "Irrigation research generates water every ten game seconds. One
      unit adds 0.25 moisture, up to 1.0; moisture decays gradually. Water only when
      get_water() is below your chosen threshold and supplies exist. A field near
      50% moisture does not need watering under a 0.3 threshold; that is expected.\n\nFertilizer
      research generates supplies on the same ten-second cycle. Fertilizer adds growth
      and infects that plant. When merged pumpkins or cacti are harvested, Weird
      Substance is proportional to the infected fraction; one infected plant cannot
      convert half the entire field. Fertilizer also performs the normal pumpkin
      death check when it reaches maturity.\n\nWeird Substance toggles infection
      on the current plot and its distinct neighbors. On a bush, enough of it creates
      a maze instead: side \xD7 2^(maze level\u22121). On treasure, the same quantity
      reuses the maze and awards gold, up to 300 reuses."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939233
    m_Localized: 07 / Giant pumpkins
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939234
    m_Localized: "A pumpkin has a 20% chance to die on reaching maturity. Scan the
      square repeatedly and replace Dead_Pumpkin cells; do not harvest healthy individual
      plants during repair. Only harvest after every cell in the desired square is
      a mature pumpkin. The game merges the largest complete square containing the
      harvest point.\n\nA side n square produces n\xB2 \xD7 min(n,6) \xD7 its per-plant
      research yield. Check the entire square, not just one ready cell. Budget seeds
      for replacement. For infection production, apply fertilizer to the number of
      mature plants you need before harvesting; read num_produced() for milestone
      progress and num_items() for spendable inventory."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444677939235
    m_Localized: 08 / Sunflower priority
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133504
    m_Localized: "measure() on a sunflower returns 7\u201315 petals. If at least
      ten sunflowers remain, harvesting the current maximum earns an 8\xD7 bonus.
      Picking a smaller flower breaks the bonus sequence until the sunflower field
      is cleared. Growing more flowers without measuring can waste most of the potential
      power.\n\nPlant the field, wait for maturity without repeatedly walking, then
      scan petal values from 15 down to 7. Research and energy accelerate instructions;
      movement and instruction execution consume power. Avoid endless full-field
      searches for each individual flower and moving loops that spend all the power
      while waiting.\n\nPower is a supply, not a permanent speed unlock. Keep a reserve
      and budget carrot inputs for the next generation of flowers."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133505
    m_Localized: 09 / Companion planting
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133506
    m_Localized: 'After companion research, get_companion() returns a requested crop
      and target coordinate, or None for an ineligible plot. Grass, bushes, trees
      and carrots can request companions. The target must contain the requested type
      when the original plant is harvested; the companion itself does not have to
      be mature.


      Read and save the request, place the companion, return to
      the original plant, then harvest when mature. Do not assume a request survives
      harvesting and replanting. Level 1 multiplies eligible harvests by 2; each
      additional level adds 0.5, reaching 4.5 at level 6. Before research there is
      no companion bonus.


      For automation, maintain a coordinate-to-request
      map and resolve conflicting requests; blindly overwriting the whole field often
      destroys useful crops.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133507
    m_Localized: 10 / Cactus sorting
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133508
    m_Localized: "Each mature cactus has a measured size from 0 to 9. swap(East)
      or swap(North) exchanges adjacent cacti. A connected mature region chains only
      when sizes are nondecreasing to the east and north. One out-of-order pair prevents
      the region-wide chain.\n\nSort every row, then every column. The shipped bubble-sort
      template is simple and reliable; optimize comparisons and movement when you
      understand its invariant. Sorting columns after rows preserves the row order.
      Chain output for m plants is per-plant yield \xD7 m \xD7 min(m,16), preserving
      a reward for larger sorted fields with bounded scaling.\n\nFund pumpkin seeds
      before clearing the previous crop. Sorting a large field before cacti mature
      does not satisfy the harvest condition."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133509
    m_Localized: 11 / Maze search
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133510
    m_Localized: 'Plant a bush, then use Weird Substance in the required quantity
      to generate a connected maze. can_move() tests walls, move() reports success,
      and measure() returns the treasure coordinate. Harvest at treasure for gold.
      Harvesting a hedge clears the maze without a treasure reward.


      Use depth-first
      search with a visited set and a direction stack. Explore unvisited neighbors;
      when stuck, reverse the last move. For reusable mazes, a visited set is essential
      because walls can be removed and loops appear. Treasure targets are chosen
      far enough along the actual passages, not at the current tile.


      At treasure,
      use Weird Substance instead of harvesting to receive gold and relocate the
      target while preserving the layout. Re-search using a fresh visited set. Reuse
      consumes supplies and is limited to 300 relocations; afterwards harvest and
      generate a new maze.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133511
    m_Localized: 12 / Long-tail routes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133512
    m_Localized: "The Dinosaur Hat enables the apple-and-tail mode. Apples consume
      cactus inventory. The tail occupies cells, prevents crossing itself, and disables
      field wrapping. can_move() and move() obey tail occupancy; measure() at the
      apple provides the next target. Only one drone can control the tail.\n\nAn
      even-sided empty field supports a Hamiltonian cycle: cover every tile along
      a nonintersecting route and return along the first column. Follow the cycle
      instead of greedily heading for each apple. Keep at least side\xB2+1 cactus
      available. Stop or switch to Straw_Hat to settle the current tail.\n\nBone
      = floor(length \xD7 min(length,64) \xD7 (1 + 0.25\xD7(research level\u22121))).
      After length 64, each extra segment still adds production, while the length
      multiplier stays bounded. The template ends when its full route becomes blocked."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133513
    m_Localized: 13 / Independent drones
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133514
    m_Localized: 'Parallel research raises capacity from 1 to 2, 4, 8, 16 and 32.
      The main controller uses a slot. spawn_drone(function,args...) returns a handle
      or None if capacity is full. Workers get independent copies of variables and
      collections, but share the field and inventory. They can occupy the same cell
      without collision.


      Use per-column or per-region jobs to avoid two workers
      planting the same plot or racing for seeds. Save handles, then wait_for() each
      result. has_finished() checks without waiting. Modifying a worker''s global
      variable does not update the controller''s copy; return a value instead. Completed
      workers release slots.


      When spawning fails, let the main controller
      perform the job. A program that never joins or terminates its workers will
      not finish a resource competition.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133515
    m_Localized: 14 / Experiments & races
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133516
    m_Localized: "Create a module named experiment. simulate(name,unlocks,items,globals,seed,speedup)
      runs a separate farm and returns game seconds. Unlocks means all research;
      dictionaries can select research levels. Input items and globals are isolated
      copies. Repeating a nonnegative seed reproduces the same initial randomness.
      Actual inventory and crops are unchanged. A simulation is capped at one game
      hour; nested simulations are unsupported.\n\nResource competitions use a standard
      8\xD78 mid-tier farm and seed 41 with supplied inputs. Targets differ: hay
      4096, wood 6000, carrots 2048, pumpkins 12000, power 8000, cactus 20000, gold
      4096, bone 30000. Produce the target AND terminate all workers. _Single categories
      restrict capacity to one. Resource challenges allow one game hour; Fastest_Reset
      starts from zero and allows four, ending when local competition research is
      purchased.\n\nRecords stay on this computer. Old-rule scores are marked historical
      and are not compared with current scores. Achievements and successful challenges
      open a completion notice; unread notices survive restarting. There is no online
      Steam submission."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133517
    m_Localized: 15 / Diagnose & recover
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133518
    m_Localized: 'Crop never appears: check its research, seed inventory, soil and
      whether the cell is empty. A failed plant() returns False; waiting on an empty
      plot cannot mature it.


      Research stays locked with enough funds: read
      the next-level crop discovery and cumulative-production requirements. Speed
      and yield tiers no longer all unlock together.


      Pumpkins never merge:
      inspect every cell for dead or immature plants. Cactus chains fail: find an
      east/north inversion or an immature member. Power disappears: stop repeated
      walking and reduce scans. Maze gets stuck: use visited and backtracking; normal
      wrapping does not apply. Drone globals do not return: use wait_for() return
      values.


      Use F9 breakpoints, Pause and Step to inspect one line at a
      time. Syntax errors include line numbers. Save backups end with .bak. Farm
      Library creates independent saves and program folders. External editor mode
      exports .py and __builtins__.py hints, then watches saves; avoid editing a
      file in two editors simultaneously. Audio level is saved when you release the
      slider.


      Full progression after an update is best tested on a new farm.
      Updating does not take back resources earned under earlier balance rules.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133519
    m_Localized: 16 / API reference
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133520
    m_Localized: 'All public game APIs are listed below with prerequisites and return
      values. Entities, Items, Grounds, Unlocks, Hats and Leaderboards are namespaces.
      Calls are case-sensitive. Successful research is paid from shared inventory.
      A cost may exist even when its discovery or production requirements are unmet.
      A fully researched node returns None for cost and requirements.


      Examples
      in other chapters may be fragments intended for an existing field or loop;
      each chapter names its assumptions. Templates provide complete algorithms for
      the major crop mechanics.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133521
    m_Localized: Harvest a mature crop; at treasure, award gold. Immature/empty plots
      return False.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133522
    m_Localized: Test maturity at the current plot; does not harvest.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133523
    m_Localized: Planting/crop research and seed inputs required; False if occupied
      or wrong ground.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133524
    m_Localized: Switch grassland and soil; use before planting soil crops.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133525
    m_Localized: Move North/East/South/West; walls and tails may block it. Ordinary
      fields wrap.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133526
    m_Localized: Sensors. Test the same walls/tail rules without moving.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133527
    m_Localized: Consume Water, Fertilizer or Weird_Substance; False if unsuitable
      or insufficient.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133528
    m_Localized: Sensors. Zero-based position and current field side length.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133529
    m_Localized: Sensors. Return an entity, None, or the ground namespace value.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133530
    m_Localized: Sensors. Current moisture in [0,1].
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133531
    m_Localized: Sensors. Spendable current inventory, shared between drones.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133532
    m_Localized: Sensors. Cumulative successfully produced amount; spending does
      not reduce it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133533
    m_Localized: Purchased level of the named research.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133534
    m_Localized: Costs. Entity gives planting inputs; Unlocks gives next research
      cost. Optional level is zero-based purchased-level index.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133535
    m_Localized: Costs. Keys unlock:<id> and produced:<item> give required discovery
      levels and cumulative production. Does not include payable price.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133536
    m_Localized: Costs. True only when discoveries, production totals and funds all
      suffice.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133537
    m_Localized: Automatic research. Pay and purchase the next level; missing requirements
      return False with no payment.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133538
    m_Localized: Sensors and companion research. Returns (entity, (x,y)) for eligible
      plants.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133539
    m_Localized: Sensors. Flower petals/cactus size; maze treasure or next-apple
      coordinates. None when unsupported.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133540
    m_Localized: Exchange adjacent cactus cells; does not buy seeds.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133541
    m_Localized: Parallel research. Independent memory copy; None when slots are
      full.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133542
    m_Localized: Wait and return the worker result; the field and other workers keep
      advancing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133543
    m_Localized: Check a worker without blocking.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133544
    m_Localized: Count active workers, including the main task, and available capacity.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133545
    m_Localized: Simulation research. Isolated program execution; fixed seed reproduces
      its starting randomness.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133546
    m_Localized: Local competition research. Run a named program in a fixed preset
      and record success after termination.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133547
    m_Localized: Timing tools. Current world seconds / this drone's instruction cost
      count.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133548
    m_Localized: World testing tools. Temporarily resize to an already purchased
      maximum; restored when execution ends. 0 means maximum.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133549
    m_Localized: World testing tools. Cap current execution speed; does not exceed
      purchased speed.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133550
    m_Localized: Select a hat; Dinosaur_Hat and Top_Hat require their research. Leaving
      tail mode settles bone.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133551
    m_Localized: Numeric utilities. Seeded uniform value in [0,1).
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133552
    m_Localized: Debugging. Write to the journal. Frequent print adds execution cost.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133553
    m_Localized: clear resets the current field and loses standing plants. do_a_flip
      consumes an action without moving.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133554
    m_Localized: " files \xB7 "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133555
    m_Localized: ' active'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1040444682133556
    m_Localized: Sensors. Cumulative harvested production, including harvested Weird
      Substance; spending does not reduce it. Passive water/fertilizer supplies use
      num_items().
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1076756604772352
    m_Localized: Enter a program name.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1076756604772353
    m_Localized: This name is reserved. Choose another name.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1076756604772354
    m_Localized: Use Chinese characters, letters, digits or underscores, up to 80
      characters. Do not add .py.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1076756604772355
    m_Localized: This program name already exists. Names cannot differ only by letter
      case.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1076756604772356
    m_Localized: "Chinese or digits may come first, for example 123, 1_farm or \u6D47\u6C34\u7A0B\u5E8F.
      At least one program is kept."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1076756604772357
    m_Localized: "Program names may start with Chinese characters or digits: 123,
      1_farm and \u6D47\u6C34\u7A0B\u5E8F are valid. Use letters, digits or underscores,
      up to 80 characters, without .py. Duplicate names, including case-only variants,
      are rejected. Import a numeric file with from 123 import work or import 123
      as farm. Chinese module names work directly, for example import \u6D47\u6C34\u7A0B\u5E8F.\n\nPrograms
      are reusable modules. The library shows a card for every file, a total count,
      active-file count and drone-slot usage. Green means the file has running workers;
      an amber border means it is open in the main editor. A file may be both running
      and selected. Paused tasks remain active; idle files have no live workers.\n\nEdit
      switches the main editor without stopping existing work. Main Run replaces
      the current controller and its workers. Window opens a draggable editor; Run
      separately launches that file if a drone slot is free. Stop all terminates
      every worker. Closing an editor window leaves its code and running tasks intact.
      Running files cannot be deleted; at least one file is retained.\n\nUse Cmd/Ctrl+Z
      to undo and Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+Z to redo. F9 toggles a breakpoint at the caret
      line. Pause, Step and the variable watch help diagnose a program."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1108438481362944
    m_Localized: 'VERDANT

      CIRCUIT'
