      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126610
    m_Localized: "3\xD73 hulls need the broad crossing; small craft can use the shortcut."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126611
    m_Localized: A network that endures
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126612
    m_Localized: Maintain reserves across six islands while shipping finished cores.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126613
    m_Localized: Verdant concord
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126614
    m_Localized: Complete a synchronized multi-product delivery. Your algorithm runs
      the archipelago.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126615
    m_Localized: Create modular example (10 files)
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126616
    m_Localized: 'Hull / programs / flights: '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126617
    m_Localized: Bind + run
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126618
    m_Localized: Stop code
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126619
    m_Localized: 'island code workers: '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126620
    m_Localized: 17 / Specialist fleets
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126621
    m_Localized: "Open Islands after discovering Carrots. The charter costs 100 Wood
      and 100 Carrots, and grants 100 fleet credits once. Island machines are separate
      from the legacy 1\u201332 crop-script workers. Three independent research tracks
      govern fleet slots (3\u20138), hull footprint (1\xD71, 2\xD71, 2\xD72, 3\xD72,
      3\xD73, including rotated variants), and specialisms. A larger hull processes
      a larger batch and carries more, but moves more slowly and must fit every occupied
      cell. Irrigators pump water; growers produce grain or medicine; engineers mine
      and refine ore/alloy or assemble cores; scouts refine crystal; haulers move
      cargo; harvesters accelerate grain production.\n\nOrders pay fleet credits.
      Each role and hull has an explicit order gate. Dismantling a landed machine
      returns its full paid hull cost; cancellation refunds reserved recipe inputs
      and uncollected cargo. In-flight machines must land before cancellation or
      dismantling. Automatic routes wait without fees; unsafe manual fleet_step moves
      trigger an emergency brake and a bounded repair fee. A footprint never overlaps
      another machine. Avoid blocking ports with manually parked machines."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126622
    m_Localized: 18 / Islands, recipes & orders
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126623
    m_Localized: 'Six local depots form a production graph: Hearth grows grain; Reed
      supplies water; Ember turns ore + grain + water into alloy; Glass needs alloy
      + water for crystal; Bloom needs grain + crystal + water for medicine; Zenith
      combines alloy + crystal + medicine into cores. Island opening requires both
      its order discovery and the corresponding main-farm discovery: Carrots / Pumpkins
      / Cactus / Mazes / Dinosaurs / Autonomy beacon. Goods are local: num_items(Items.Water)
      is not fleet_stock(island,"water").


      Use fleet_map to inspect each island
      and its graph. Broad channels form an eastbound/westbound loop; small machines
      can use narrow shortcuts. Shipments reserve real source stock when accepted,
      then a physical hauler travels to a dock, loads its hold, crosses each connected
      channel and waits for a complete landing footprint. Reserved cargo and cargo
      in flight are not available for another recipe or order.


      18 orders
      require several products and destinations simultaneously. Deliver all consumes
      the listed local stock once. Later briefs also certify actual hull use, distinct
      concurrent programs and simultaneous flights; their checklists show current
      peaks and required values. No elapsed-time certification is used. The six-island
      campaign follows the farming campaign; editing, debugging and optimal overlapping
      production can change total completion time.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126624
    m_Localized: 19 / A controller for every island
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126625
    m_Localized: "Use the Islands screen to create the 10-file modular example. island_controller
      imports island_planner; the coordinator allocates physical machines, expands
      recipe dependencies and sends jobs to individual inboxes. fleet_worker is a
      shared function library. Each island_water / island_grain / island_foundry
      / island_crystal / island_medicine / island_archive / island_cargo program
      imports that library with different allowed recipes.\n\nfleet_run(id,file)
      binds an independent interpreter to a physical machine. unit_id and the initial
      island_id are injected; fleet_self() returns the bound machine ID. A worker
      can import more files, define functions and return results. Inboxes copy message
      data, and each worker has its own variables and module state. fleet_send sends
      a job; fleet_receive receives the next message for this worker. fleet_result
      retrieves a finished result variable. One worker error stops that program and
      is shown on its card; other workers and physical queues continue. Infinite
      loops have a bounded instruction budget per simulation tick.\n\nQueued physical
      jobs, reservations and in-flight cargo are saved. Running Python call stacks,
      message inboxes and return objects are not saved. After loading, restart the
      coordinator or explicitly bind the worker program again; check existing jobs
      before sending duplicates. Stop code ends the interpreter; Cancel queue cancels
      landed physical jobs. The main farm Run button starts the coordinator, whereas
      Bind + run on a fleet card starts that machine\u2019s program."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126626
    m_Localized: 'Sign once: Carrots + 100 Wood + 100 Carrots; grants 100 fleet credits
      once.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126627
    m_Localized: Read independent slot/size/role progress, current multi-goal contract
      and physical agents. Unit snapshots include incoming shipments, pending production,
      code errors and inbox size.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126628
    m_Localized: 'Available local stock, excluding accepted shipping reservations.
      Cargo names are strings: water, grain, ore, alloy, crystal, medicine, core.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126629
    m_Localized: "Terrain rows from bottom to top, recipes, role requirements, coordinates
      and island links. Island IDs are 0\u20135."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126630
    m_Localized: Pays credits and respects independent role, hull, slot and parking-space
      limits. Rotated hulls are supported.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126631
    m_Localized: Pay fleet credits after the named order discovery. Buying slots
      does not enlarge a hull.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126632
    m_Localized: Queue a role-compatible local recipe. One batch scales inputs and
      outputs by occupied area; inputs reserve when processing begins.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126633
    m_Localized: Haulers only. Atomically reserves available source stock, then physically
      loads, flies and unloads; no instant cargo transfer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126634
    m_Localized: Queue inter-island travel or a local route. Terrain, lane direction
      and every occupied hull cell are checked.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126635
    m_Localized: Inspect a terrain-aware local path. Live reservations can make actual
      execution wait or reroute.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126636
    m_Localized: Idle machines only. Failed unsafe steps trigger emergency braking
      and at most two credits in fees. Rotation must fit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126637
    m_Localized: Landed machines only. Refund reserved inputs and uncollected manifests;
      dismantling also refunds the hull cost.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126638
    m_Localized: Consumes all current contract goals once, after hull/program/flight
      checklist conditions are met; rewards credits and discovers the next order.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126639
    m_Localized: Start an independent named-file interpreter or stop code. Stop does
      not cancel already queued physical work.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126640
    m_Localized: Bound physical machine ID inside a fleet program; -1 in the main
      controller.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126641
    m_Localized: Send a copied value to a bounded 16-message inbox. Receive is nonblocking
      and returns None when empty; only bound workers receive their own inbox.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126642
    m_Localized: Read a copied result variable from a finished program; transient
      and not saved.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126643
    m_Localized: "Yield the caller while physical queues and other programs advance;
      range 0\u20133600. Not an unlock timer."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126644
    m_Localized: Open archipelago
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126645
    m_Localized: Build an island network
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126646
    m_Localized: Research and all 18 island orders complete.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1121342031126647
    m_Localized: 'Island order '
