    m_Localized: Sign the charter and connect six local production chains.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1123447513014272
    m_Localized: 'Requires main-farm discovery: '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1134938773512192
    m_Localized: Code stopped. An active coordinator may restart it; use Stop all
      for manual control.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1134938777706496
    m_Localized: Archipelago order record
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1134938777706497
    m_Localized: "Start on one grass plot with no inventory. Grass matures naturally.
      Run harvest() until you own five hay, then research Loops. Load First harvest
      from Templates.\n\nNext research Operators, Variables, Sensors and Planting.
      Research does not happen just because you own enough resources: select a node
      and pay, or later use unlock(). Free grass and bushes provide recovery if you
      run out of crop seeds.\n\nThis campaign aims at about three hours of game time
      to full research with a working automated strategy. 0.12.1 adds the multi-hour
      six-island logistics campaign after and alongside this research route. Your
      planning and editing time is additional. Research speed bonuses are part of
      normal 1\xD7 play; the Settings speed multiplier accelerates the entire world."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1134938777706498
    m_Localized: "Use the Islands screen to create the 10-file modular example. island_controller
      imports island_planner; the coordinator allocates physical machines, expands
      recipe dependencies and sends jobs to individual inboxes. fleet_worker is a
      shared function library. Each island_water / island_grain / island_foundry
      / island_crystal / island_medicine / island_archive / island_cargo program
      imports that library with different allowed recipes.\n\nfleet_run(id,file)
      binds an independent interpreter to a physical machine. unit_id and the initial
      island_id are injected; fleet_self() returns the bound machine ID. A worker
      can import more files, define functions and return results. Inboxes copy message
      data, and each worker has its own variables and module state. fleet_send sends
      a job; fleet_receive receives the next message for this worker. fleet_result
      retrieves a finished result variable. One worker error stops that program and
      is shown on its card; other workers and physical queues continue. Infinite
      loops have a bounded instruction budget per simulation tick.\n\nQueued physical
      jobs, reservations and in-flight cargo are saved. Running Python call stacks,
      message inboxes and return objects are not saved. After loading, restart the
      coordinator or explicitly bind the worker program again; check existing jobs
      before sending duplicates. Stop code ends the interpreter; an active coordinator
      may restart it, so use Stop all before taking manual control. Cancel queue
      cancels landed physical jobs. The main farm Run button starts the coordinator,
      whereas Bind + run on a fleet card starts that machine\u2019s program."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1134938777706499
    m_Localized: Export 12
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1134938777706500
    m_Localized: "Open Islands after discovering Carrots. The charter costs 100 Wood
      and 100 Carrots, and grants 100 fleet credits once. Island machines are separate
      from the legacy 1\u201332 crop-script workers. Three independent research tracks
      govern fleet slots (3\u20138), hull footprint (1\xD71, 2\xD71, 2\xD72, 3\xD72,
      3\xD73, including rotated variants), and specialisms. A larger hull processes
      a larger batch and carries more, but moves more slowly and must fit every occupied
      cell. Irrigators pump water; growers produce grain or medicine; engineers mine
      and refine ore/alloy or assemble cores; scouts refine crystal; haulers move
      cargo; harvesters accelerate grain production.\n\nOrders pay fleet credits.
      Each role and hull has an explicit order gate. Export surplus depot goods with
      fleet_sell to recover credits after repair penalties; exports consume real
      available goods and cannot sell reserved manifests. Dismantling a landed machine
      returns its full paid hull cost; cancellation refunds reserved recipe inputs
      and uncollected cargo. In-flight machines must land before cancellation or
      dismantling. Automatic routes wait without fees; unsafe manual fleet_step moves
      trigger an emergency brake and a bounded repair fee. A footprint never overlaps
      another machine. Avoid blocking ports with manually parked machines."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1134938777706501
    m_Localized: Inspect export prices or sell real available local stock to recover
      credits. Reserved and in-flight cargo cannot be sold.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
