  - m_Id: 1262209932976158
    m_Localized: Six flowers, pollination supplies and botanical processing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976159
    m_Localized: Stone, bronze, silver, gold ore, platinum and diamonds.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976160
    m_Localized: Six fish species and fishmeal for a circular supply network.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976161
    m_Localized: World
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976162
    m_Localized: "EARTH / Home garden \u2192 island network"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976163
    m_Localized: Harvester / fisheries
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976164
    m_Localized: EARTH / ISLAND NETWORK
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976165
    m_Localized: The next chapter of your Earth garden
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976166
    m_Localized: 'Continue the cultivation route to Parallel Drones, then research
      Earth & archipelago network. Modules, Dictionaries and Irrigation are required.


      Earth
      inventory becomes your home depot. Harvested crops and power can be shipped
      to flowers, minerals and fisheries. Drone programs remain independent while
      island managers and a network program coordinate them.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976167
    m_Localized: View technology route
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976168
    m_Localized: 'One world / drones '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976169
    m_Localized: " \xB7 hull tier "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976170
    m_Localized: " \xB7 credits "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976171
    m_Localized: " \xB7 orders "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976172
    m_Localized: 'Earth farmer: original crop functions. Other specialists: named
      product functions. Transport moves actual Earth inventory.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976173
    m_Localized: Programs & bindings
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976174
    m_Localized: Product reference
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976175
    m_Localized: "Earth \xB7 Home Garden"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976176
    m_Localized: "Floralia \xB7 Flower Island"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976177
    m_Localized: "Aurelia \xB7 Mineral Island"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976178
    m_Localized: "Pelagia \xB7 Fish Island"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976179
    m_Localized: Floralia collection
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976180
    m_Localized: Supply Earth inputs and collect six botanical products.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976181
    m_Localized: The mineral ladder
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976182
    m_Localized: Advance from renewable stone to diamond refinement.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976183
    m_Localized: Pelagia fisheries
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976184
    m_Localized: Coordinate six fisheries with imported feed and flowers.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976185
    m_Localized: Earth returns
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976186
    m_Localized: Return specialist island products to the original Earth inventory.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976187
    m_Localized: A circular ocean
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976188
    m_Localized: Flowers feed fisheries; fishmeal feeds flowers; minerals support
      both.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976189
    m_Localized: One Earth, many algorithms
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976190
    m_Localized: Coordinate Earth and three specialist islands in a single supply
      network.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976191
    m_Localized: 'Choose Enter Earth on the world screen. Start with a one-plot garden
      and no inventory. Harvest free grass, learn loops, planting and sensors, then
      develop the original crop chain. At Parallel Drones, continue to Earth & archipelago
      network. Modules, Dictionaries and Irrigation are also required.


      This
      is one campaign. Earth is island 0 and its original inventory is the home depot.
      Flower, mineral and fish islands are later research branches. Physical shipping
      connects them; special-island cargo cannot appear instantly at home. Programming
      and strategy affect duration; no time certification forces you to wait.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976192
    m_Localized: 'The program center separates files from execution targets. Choose
      Earth farmer, Network, Island manager, a specific drone or a named group. Edit
      changes only the file being viewed. Bind only saves a target association and
      stops its old code; Bind + run starts the selected file on that target. One
      drone, island or network target has at most one active interpreter. Different
      targets run concurrently.


      Green cards are active, amber borders mark
      the edited file, and binding labels list target IDs. Files used by a running
      program or imported library cannot be deleted. At least one file remains. Chinese
      and numeric names are accepted; imports use the file name without .py.


      The
      studio target strip shows what Run affects. Floating editors also run on this
      selected target. Stop target leaves other targets running; Stop all stops managers,
      workers and landed physical work. Undo/redo, independent editor windows and
      external editing remain available.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976193
    m_Localized: "Earth farmers run original crop functions against the same Earth
      field and inventory. Each bound farmer has its own coordinates and variables.
      Permanent workers are created with fleet_build and bound with program_bind/program_run.
      Legacy spawn_drone(function,args...) creates a temporary farmer from an Earth
      worker; completion releases its slot and wait_for returns its value.\n\nFor
      groups use group_create(name,[ids...]) and group_run(name,file). Members execute
      independent copies of the file; fleet_self identifies the current member. They
      do not share mutable variables. Use inbox messages to coordinate. Managers
      consume no physical drone slot. Farmer bodies are 1\xD71; specialist hulls
      use the researched rectangular traffic system. Earth crop workers retain the
      original overflight behavior on the crop grid."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976194
    m_Localized: 21 / Every product function
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976195
    m_Localized: "Each named product function queues work on its designated island.
      It does not create output immediately. Batch input and output multiply by hull
      area. Use the recipe table below; batch seconds are base 1\xD71 values. Gold
      ore is gold_ore and is separate from treasure coins (gold). Bronze is a processed
      alloy, not a raw natural ore. Fish hatchery batches represent managed fisheries
      rather than instant catches."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976196
    m_Localized: 22 / Every network function
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976197
    m_Localized: 'Reference entries specify arguments, results, requirements, failure
      behavior and examples. Pass the stable drone ID returned by fleet_build, not
      its list position. Island managers use island_self; workers use fleet_self.
      Checking a queue and accepting a command are different from completion.


      The
      API uses positional arguments only. Examples mentioning drone_id or hauler
      require an existing machine ID. Files must already exist in Programs.


      Inventory
      calls return available stock. Unit snapshots expose job counts, cargo, flight
      status, program state and errors.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976198
    m_Localized: 24 / Local races & records
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976199
    m_Localized: Local races remain available from Records. They use preset independent
      farms with a fixed seed; finish the requested production and terminate the
      program to record a result. Historical rules are labeled separately. The simulation
      laboratory, its research and simulate() have been removed. Existing live farms
      are not reset by a race.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976200
    m_Localized: Bind
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976201
    m_Localized: 'TARGET / '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976202
    m_Localized: " \xB7 change"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976203
    m_Localized: Earth & archipelago network
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976204
    m_Localized: Flower island
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976205
    m_Localized: Mineral island
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976206
    m_Localized: Fish island
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976207
    m_Localized: ' / started'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976208
    m_Localized: ' / bound'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976209
    m_Localized: Home inventory
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976210
    m_Localized: 25 / Namespaces & inventory IDs
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976211
    m_Localized: "Entities selects original Earth crops; Items selects inventory
      resources; Unlocks selects research, never a crop seed. North/East/South/West
      are directions, Grounds selects terrain, Hats selects appearance or exploration
      behavior, and Leaderboards selects local race categories.\n\nUse string cargo
      IDs with fleet_stock, fleet_ship and product_info. Items.Rose is equivalent
      to 'rose', Items.Gold_Ore to 'gold_ore', while Items.Gold remains treasure
      currency. Island IDs are stable: Earth 0; logistics outposts 1\u20135; Flowers
      6, Minerals 7, Fish 8. Drone IDs are allocated separately and are not island
      IDs.\n\nSave stores physical inventory, jobs, reservations, bindings, groups
      and unread notices. Call stacks, messages and results are transient. Existing
      home and island-0 warehouses merge once on upgrade. Back up your farm before
      comparing old versions."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1262209932976212
    m_Localized: EARTH INVENTORY / original crops and returned island products
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1263414637748224
    m_Localized: 17 / Unified drones & traffic
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1263414641942528
    m_Localized: 'All persistent machines appear in one fleet list, including Earth
      farmers. Slot capacity follows purchased parallel-drone research and fleet
      slot upgrades. Count, hull area and role research are independent. A bigger
      machine scales recipe inputs and output by area; duration scales more slowly,
      but the body needs wider lanes.


      Physical jobs are queued, up to 64
      per drone. Broad passages use a one-way loop, smaller hulls can take narrow
      shortcuts, and docking/landing reserves the full footprint. Unsafe manual movement
      may incur repair fees; automatic routes wait or yield rather than overlap.
      Engineer research opens after order 6 or Mineral Island; harvester after order
      7 or Fish Island. Ordinary recipe work requires its assigned role.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1263414641942529
    m_Localized: 19 / Managers, workers & modules
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1263414641942530
    m_Localized: 'Create the unified example from Programs. Bind unified_controller
      to Network. It starts earth_manager and the unlocked flower/mineral/fish managers,
      then terminates. The managers and workers continue independently. Each island
      has at most one manager; every drone keeps its own file binding. Re-running
      a manager reuses a matching drone and may restart that worker, so inspect existing
      jobs before adding work.


      Specialist workers import production_helpers
      and enqueue one batch when idle. Arrange real deliveries first: rose needs
      water and compost, carp needs hay and water. Managers may fail to build if
      all slots are occupied; free a slot, research more capacity or reassign a machine.
      The example teaches hierarchy and does not automatically complete every order.


      Physical
      queues, cargo and bindings are saved. Interpreter stacks, inboxes and results
      are not. After loading, restart the appropriate controller; stopping a parent
      does not recursively stop children. Worker errors are isolated, shown on its
      card and program_state. CPU budgets keep a tight loop from freezing other interpreters.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1264237723770880
    m_Localized: 18 / One Earth supply network
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1264237723770881
    m_Localized: 'Earth (0) uses the original inventory, not a second warehouse.
      fleet_stock(0,''wood'') and num_items(Items.Wood) agree. Orders, exports, crop
      planting and research compete for the same available Earth resources. Transport
      reserves stock at acceptance, carries limited holds across actual flights,
      and unloads once. Returning an island product to Earth makes it available in
      the original home inventory.


      The five original logistics outposts remain
      as stepping stones. Three new research branches open Floralia (6), Aurelia
      (7) and Pelagia (8) independently. Query world_islands and check unlocked;
      do not assume all numbers below the unlocked count are open. New six-product
      contracts follow the original logistics orders, ending with synchronized returns
      to Earth.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1264237723770882
    m_Localized: "20 / Earth \u2192 three islands"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1264237723770883
    m_Localized: '1. Enter Earth; complete the original crop and language discoveries.

      2.
      Research Parallel Drones, Modules, Dictionaries and Irrigation. Purchase Earth
      & archipelago network for 500 treasure gold. There is no second charter fee.

      3.
      Research Flower Island (2000 pumpkin), Mineral Island (5000 cactus), or Fish
      Island (20000 carrot). The branches are independent.

      4. Build the appropriate
      specialist and a hauler, respecting slot capacity.

      5. Bind and run programs;
      transport real inputs before waiting for outputs.

      6. Return products
      to Earth, complete orders and expand the network.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1264237723770884
    m_Localized: 23 / Control patterns & recovery
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1264237723770885
    m_Localized: 'Direct: call grow_rose(id,4) from a manager. Bound: program_bind(id,''rose_worker''),
      then program_run(id). Group: group_create(''team'',[a,b]), then group_run(''team'',''worker'').
      Module: import production_helpers; each interpreter gets its own module variables.
      Message: fleet_send(id, payload), then fleet_receive inside that worker. Results:
      assign result in a finite worker and read fleet_result(id).


      For mixed
      products, bind different files, branch on fleet_self/island_self, or receive
      a message with the requested recipe. A productive circular chain starts with
      basic carp and lavender before lotus and koi; gold_ore needs bronze and silver,
      platinum needs roses, diamonds need orchids.


      If production waits: check
      product_info inputs, local stock, reservations, the correct role and unlocked
      island. If traffic waits: inspect hull footprint and docking; cancel landed
      jobs before reassigning. If a manager keeps restarting a worker, stop the manager
      or Stop all before editing assignments.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
