    m_Localized: Ocean planet
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176149
    m_Localized: 01 / Enter the universe
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176150
    m_Localized: Only Earth is initially unlocked. Enter Earth, run harvest() after
      the first grass matures, and pay for Loops, Planting and Sensors. The original
      Earth crop progression is retained; Spaceflight is a later discovery. Other
      planets begin at one native plot when researched. This version uses a separate
      Universe0131 save directory so the previous live game is preserved.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176151
    m_Localized: 02 / Spherical coordinates
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176152
    m_Localized: "Earth is the original farm on a sphere, not a second garden. Expansion
      stages are 1\xD71,2\xD72,4\xD74,8\xD78,16\xD716,32\xD732,64\xD764,128\xD7128,256\xD7128,360\xD7128.
      Each cell spans one degree. Full latitude coverage is the belt -64\xB0 to+64\xB0,
      excluding both poles. Only a fully unlocked 360-column surface wraps longitude;
      latitude never wraps. Expansion centers the old patch, keeps plants and shifts
      local coordinates. Read current coordinates after expanding. Use get_world_width
      and get_world_height separately."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176153
    m_Localized: 03 / Research & expansion
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176154
    m_Localized: "Original crop discoveries gate Earth expansion, speed and yield.
      The last four Earth expansion tiers need Spaceflight, Flower Planet, Mineral
      Planet and Ocean Planet. Buy Spaceflight after Parallel Drones, Modules, Dictionaries
      and Irrigation. Flower Planet costs2000 pumpkin; Ocean Planet20000 carrot;
      Mineral Planet5000 cactus. Exterior surfaces expand using local produce: price20\xD7next
      stage squared, paid in rose,carp or stone. No elapsed-time certificate forces
      a wait."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176155
    m_Localized: 04 / Original Earth crops
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176156
    m_Localized: 'Keep original crop mechanics: tree spacing, companions, water and
      infection; giant pumpkin squares, dead replacements; sunflower petal priority;
      sorted cactus regions; connected mazes; dinosaur tails and bone settlement.
      Treasure produces coins, while gold is a refined mineral. Crop movement now
      respects spherical edges. Re-read rectangular extents and reset to the beginning
      after a sweep. Expanded grids preserve planted crops.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176157
    m_Localized: 05 / Python-inspired language
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176158
    m_Localized: The game interpreter is a documented subset, not system Python.
      It supports loops, conditionals, functions, closures, defaults, positional
      arguments, collections, modules and return values. It has no OS/file/network/stdlib
      access, exceptions or keyword arguments. New sum/enumerate/zip/sorted/reversed/round/all/any/pow/divmod/type/Unicode
      helpers and string methods are documented individually. Collection operations
      return snapshots rather than Python lazy iterators/views. Numbers use a shared
      numeric representation.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176159
    m_Localized: 06 / Program targets
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176160
    m_Localized: Top navigation opens Universe, Colony, Research, Programs, Manual,
      UFO, Records and Settings. Program center targets and files scroll independently.
      A worker, a planet manager and the universe controller each have at most one
      interpreter. Bind only stops and associates; Bind+run starts. Browsing another
      file never replaces running code. Green means running; an amber border means
      editing. At least one file remains. Numeric and Chinese file names are supported.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176161
    m_Localized: 07 / Native craft & hulls
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176162
    m_Localized: "Earth has drones, Floralia bees, Pelagia fishing boats, Aurelia
      mining drones. They cannot change planets. Each planet has separate slotTier
      and hullTier variables; both require paid local research. Hulls1\xD71,2\xD71,2\xD72,3\xD72,3\xD73
      occupy real cells and must fit unlocked space. Worker paths reserve full footprints
      and queue when blocked. Bees flap wings, drones spin rotors, boats animate
      propellers and mining drones animate drills."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176163
    m_Localized: 08 / Floralia botanical colony
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176164
    m_Localized: "Bees manage rose,tulip,lavender,lily,orchid and lotus batches;
      honey is collected from rose resources. Rose works on the first plot, tulip/lavender
      need width2, and lily/orchid/lotus width4. Water and compost arrive by UFO.
      Orchids need refined silver; lotus needs fishmeal. Inputs and outputs scale
      with hull area, while batch time uses0.8+0.2\xD7sqrt(area)."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176165
    m_Localized: 09 / Pelagia fisheries
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176166
    m_Localized: 'Boats catch carp,trout,salmon,cod,tuna and koi using fish feed;
      koi also require lotus. Shoals are spatial: planet_scan reveals the species
      and a boat navigates to a matching accessible cell before processing. More
      species become available as the surface expands. Fishmeal processes caught
      carp. None of these functions creates free fish without input or time.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176167
    m_Localized: 10 / Aurelia mining & refining
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176168
    m_Localized: Mining produces stone, copper_ore,tin_ore,silver_ore,gold_ore,platinum_ore
      and rough_diamond. Native drones navigate to matching deposits. Smelting produces
      copper,tin,bronze,silver,gold; platinum is refined and diamond is cut. Bronze
      consumes3 copper+1 tin+solar energy, not stone. Platinum needs roses and diamond
      cutting needs orchids. Deposits are renewable batch sources in this edition;
      energy is consumed for each mining/refining batch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176169
    m_Localized: 11 / UFO freight & energy
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176170
    m_Localized: "Only UFOs move items between planets. Build costs50 credits+20wood+10solar
      energy on Earth and provides120 battery. Launch atomically reserves full stock
      and battery: ceil(amount/capacity)\xD7(2+planet-ID distance). Each flight leg
      lasts12+6\xD7planet-ID distance seconds. Capacities24,72,144,288 and1\u20134
      ships are researched independently using returned bronze/silver/platinum. Refuel
      at the current dock with local solar energy:5 battery/unit, maximum1000. Cancel
      refunds unused stock immediately; airborne cargo finishes its current leg and
      deposits at destination."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176171
    m_Localized: 12 / Local swarms & messages
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176172
    m_Localized: swarm_create names unique worker IDs from one planet. Several groups
      may coexist, and one file can run as independent copies. Variables and module
      instances are isolated; messages are deep-copied and inboxes hold16 values.
      fleet_receive is nonblocking and returns None when empty. Use separate planet
      managers and a universe program to coordinate different swarms.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176173
    m_Localized: 13 / Controller hierarchy
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176174
    m_Localized: Create the 11-file universe example. Run universe_controller on
      Universe; it launches managers for unlocked planets. Each manager binds its
      native starter worker. Parent completion does not stop children. Managers do
      not consume worker slots. Worker errors stop only that interpreter. Physical
      work queues may continue after code stops; use worker_cancel or stop_all deliberately.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176175
    m_Localized: 14 / Saves, compatibility & debugging
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176176
    m_Localized: 0.13.1 saves are isolated under Automation/Universe0131. Old farm
      files are retained and not silently converted into a different universe. Save
      physical cargo, queues, battery, surfaces, swarms and file bindings. Interpreter
      stacks,inboxes and result objects are transient; restart controllers after
      loading and inspect existing queues. Original race farms remain separate. Ctrl/Cmd+Z
      undo, Shift+Ctrl/Cmd+Z redo, F9 breakpoints and external editing remain.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176177
    m_Localized: 15 / Earth & Python reference
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176178
    m_Localized: Every retained Earth function and Python-inspired helper has an
      individual entry below, including defaults, results and examples. Keys are
      case-sensitive. No keyword arguments. get_world_size is a compatibility width
      query, not a rectangular height.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176179
    m_Localized: 16 / Universe, workers & UFO API
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176180
    m_Localized: Use universe_ for global management, planet_ for a colony, worker_
      for native craft, swarm_ for local groups and ufo_ exclusively for interplanetary
      freight. Kept fleet_/island_ names are compatibility spellings and are documented
      separately. fleet_ship and fleet_rebase are retired, not teleport shortcuts.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176181
    m_Localized: 17 / Every production function
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1280139257176182
    m_Localized: Each product function maps to exactly one native recipe. It enqueues
      work, never an immediate free item. The recipe table below is exported from
      the runtime. Distinguish coins, gold_ore and gold; raw minerals and refined
      products are separate inventory IDs.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1281174193299456
    m_Localized: Worker
    m_Metadata:
